{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CefsNULFcUNCZs4sd43z1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LsD5EaCnESU5TxQiYTxWh2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template-drive/memory/reworked-lane-residue-and-driven-verification.md","content":"---\nname: reworked-lane-residue-and-driven-verification\ndescription: A killed session's uncommitted residue can carry a figure it never ran; and driving a rework fix (not re-reading it) is what finds the defect the fix missed\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nTwo things that both bit on the WI-579 rework lane (2026-09-02) and generalize\nto any resumed worker session.\n\n**Uncommitted residue can contain an unproduced measurement.** Session 010 wrote\nthe full-suite figure into the archived spec *ahead of* the run, said so plainly\nin its own session log, then ended before running it. The number survived as\nworking-tree residue, where nothing distinguishes a written figure from a\nmeasured one. When reconciling `git status` on a resumed lane, grep the residue\nfor figures and cross-check each against the prior session's log before\ncommitting it — the prior session's own words are the evidence.\n\n**Verify a rework fix by DRIVING it, not by re-reading it.** Re-reading the\nround-007 finding-2 fix showed it correct. Driving it on a git fixture found a\nfifth defect of the same family: the refresh peel was tip-only (it is shared\nwith a `reset --hard`, where peeling too far destroys work), so a *record-only*\ntelemetry commit stacked on a refresh buried the peel and moved the identity the\nfold exists to keep still. Both readers then agreed on the wrong answer.\n\n**Why:** a fix that unifies two readers can still leave a third writer, or a\nneighbouring commit class, choosing its own answer — and that is invisible to\nreading, because each piece reads correctly on its own.\n\n**How to apply:** after any \"one definition, two readers\" fix, enumerate the\ncommit classes (work / record / refresh / merge / empty) and drive at least the\nadjacent ones. When the driven answer contradicts the spec's Deliverable, fix\nthe code and say so — do not ship the claim. See\n[[rederive-dont-rerun-measured-claims]] and\n[[stale-not-discharged-clauses-on-approved-rows]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1674,"cache_read_input_tokens":164967,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1674},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"53a723b2-64b3-4f77-9ded-093776f09ece","uuid":"00bd0d8e-7b3a-4210-855b-840a2d41c44f","request_id":"req_011CefsNTWPvjQJ3PGNBdezT"}
