{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CefsQUAPrsAaW1JbR6vQm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Lane closed and green. Four commits this session.\n\n## What I found first\n\nThe four round-007 findings were **already fixed** by session 010 (`6136cdcc`). But that session was killed before it finished, leaving residue — and the residue contained a full-suite figure it had **explicitly said it hadn't run**:\n\n> *\"One thing I have not yet done and will not claim until I see it: the archived spec currently carries placeholder full-suite figures I wrote ahead of the run.\"*\n\nThe placeholder was sitting in the archived spec as an uncommitted edit, where nothing distinguishes a written number from a measured one. I retracted it (`025a0643`), ran the suite, and committed the real figure (`863e768e`). The guessed counts happened to be right; the seconds weren't.\n\n## The fifth defect\n\nVerifying finding 2's fix by **driving** it rather than re-reading it turned up a defect of the same family — the row's own failure mode:\n\n`work_tip` peels a refresh sitting *literally* on the tip, and must: it's shared with the `reset --hard` in `integrate.refresh`, where peeling one commit too far destroys work. `governing_identity` reused that peel. So a **telemetry commit** — `docs/iteration/`, one of the three `RECORD_PREFIXES` the fold exists to ignore — moved the governing identity anyway, by *hiding* the refresh:\n\n| state | governing | loop `owed` | gate |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| round served, no refresh | `4fff62ba…` | False | merges |\n| refresh on the tip (what round 007 tested) | `4fff62ba…` | False | merges |\n| **+ one telemetry commit on top** | `f2bca684…` | **True** | **refuses** |\n\nBoth readers agreeing on the wrong answer, an honest APPROVE parked at a supervisor stop by the process writing about itself. That is OI-76 in one sentence, one commit further down than round 007 reached.\n\nThe fix does **not** widen `work_tip` — that would trade a stale verdict for destroyed work. `governing_rev` is a separate read-only walk. The regression pins its opposite too (a work commit above the refresh *does* re-owe), and I verified it bites: reverting to `work_tip` fails it.\n\n## Bars\n\n- Full suite at `cee19210`: **3343 passed, 24 skipped, 1 failed in 615.27s** — the one failure is the trunk-owned `docs/stage` fingerprint, already bisected clean at this branch's base and recorded as a finding this row raised and did not fix.\n- Smoke: 1504 passed / 8 skipped, 29.5s vs the 60s ceiling. `check.py --jobs 0`: **RESULT: PASS**.\n\nSpine rows LLR-207 / IF-175 / TC-205 amended (all `Drafted` — **no Status flipped**, no approval act), approval brief regenerated. Final commit `86e0c9c4` carries `WI: WI-579`.\n\n**The branch now owes a fresh review round** — the tree changed after round 007, which is the gate working as designed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":340,"cache_read_input_tokens":168262,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":340},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"53a723b2-64b3-4f77-9ded-093776f09ece","uuid":"7ff10ca2-3aba-4305-93d4-886b93c91ffe","request_id":"req_011CefsQTMH6oi5WwosduhsZ"}
